<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}" dir="{{ direction }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}{{ copy.product }}{% endblock %}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ assets }}/shell.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ assets }}/shell-components.css">
</head>
<body data-language="{{ language }}">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">{{ copy.skip }}</a>
  {#
    The persistent frame. It degrades by surface rather than rendering one fixed row, because
    `_unavailable` and `_no_membership` are handed nothing but a language -- "takes no cause, so it
    can disclose none" -- and `StrictUndefined` would turn an unconditional `organization_name` into
    a 500 on the two surfaces that exist to absorb failure.

    So the brand and the language control, which need only `language`, are on every surface, and the
    organization and `Team` appear where a resolved organization was passed. That is `FR-050` holding
    by construction rather than by care: `unavailable` never receives the context, so its frame is
    the same whichever cause brought the reader there.

    `Team` is the only destination. `FR-049` forbids rendering an entry for a surface with no
    implementation, and the dispatcher answers exactly two.
  #}
  <header class="shell-identity">
    <a class="brand" href="{{ prefix }}/{{ language }}" aria-label="{{ copy.frame_home_label }}">
      <span>KHEPRI</span>
    </a>
    {% if organization_name is defined and organization_name %}
    {#
      Named by both spans in source order, so the accessible name is "Acme Trading Change
      organization" rather than a bare organization name whose purpose a screen reader cannot infer.
      `dir="ltr"` on the name itself: `FR-055` requires a Latin run inside Arabic prose to carry its
      direction, and an organization name is the most likely Latin run on this surface.
    #}
    <a class="frame-organization"
       href="{{ prefix }}/{{ language }}"
       aria-labelledby="frame-organization-name frame-organization-action">
      <span id="frame-organization-name" dir="ltr">{{ organization_name }}</span>
      <span id="frame-organization-action" class="visually-hidden">{{ copy.frame_organization_label }}</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="frame-surfaces" aria-label="{{ copy.team_title }}">
      <a href="{{ prefix }}/{{ language }}/{{ organization_id }}/team">{{ copy.team_title }}</a>
    </nav>
    {% endif %}
    {#
      `FR-047` makes the language a property of the address, so this swaps the segment and keeps the
      surface -- scenario 11's "language switch mid-surface, position preserved". `lang` is set so a
      screen reader pronounces the target language in that language rather than in the page's.
    #}
    <a class="frame-language"
       href="{{ prefix }}/{{ alternate }}{{ surface_path }}"
       lang="{{ copy.frame_language_code }}">{{ copy.frame_language }}</a>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content" class="shell-main" tabindex="-1">
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
  </main>
</body>
</html>
